 "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =4\\sqrt{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\text{i}\\,\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3}{2}+\\text{i}\\,\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =6+2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78277b67c5ea3cc29d1be4bffc13aa6605e41ff3e33d0eae06dbef12541c60e5"} {"question" "q-321310" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321310" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321310" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321310" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=\\frac{9}{5+2\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** value of $r$ and round $\\theta $ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi )$ to **two decimal places**.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (cos$\n$(${{field-2}}$)$\n$+\\,isin$\n$(${{field-3}}$))$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $5-2\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{9}{5+2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9(5-2\\text{i})}{(5+2\\text{i})(5-2\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{45-18\\text{i}}{{5}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{45-18\\text{i}}{{5}^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{45-18\\text{i}}{29} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{29}-\\frac{18}{29}\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{45}{29}-\\frac{18}{29}\\,i,$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{45}{29})}^{2}+{(\\frac{18}{29})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2025+324}{{29}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2349}}{29} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{29}}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{45}{29}$ and $y=-\\frac{18}{29},$ $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -arctan\\,(\\frac{|y|}{x}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -arctan\\,(\\frac{18}{45}) \\\\  & ≈5.90\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{9\\sqrt{29}}{29}\\cdot \\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5.90)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5.90)).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78277b67c5ea3cc29d1be4bffc13aa6605e41ff3e33d0eae06dbef12541c60e5"} {"question" "q-321385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1265941382a9e43f43d1d5106323af10025"} {"question" "q-321385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\sqrt{29}}{29}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994893/state.json" "file_sha256" "da5290772662786589f59487e0c5d1